<%# Owner-only "Edit your profile" modal — faithful port of the legacy SPA
    `User/form.js`, minus the email field (email stays API-only).

    The `dialog` controller drives the native <dialog> open/close/backdrop/
    focus-restore. Photo upload is a plain multipart `file_field :avatar` (no JS
    widget). The PATCH form posts to /u/:username and comes back as a Turbo Stream
    (update.turbo_stream.erb) that refreshes the header and fires `close_dialog`.

    Locals: user. Optional: open (true renders the dialog inline for the no-JS
    /u/:username/edit fallback page).

    TRIGGER (Hoojah 2026 redesign, Phase 4, Task 4.4): the trigger used to be a
    bare pencil, absolutely positioned top-right of the header card. It now sits
    inline in the gradient hero's action bar (`users/_profile_header`), so THIS
    partial no longer positions itself — the caller wraps it. The trigger icon is
    now `settings` (a gear, matching the mockup's action bar), not `edit`; the
    `aria-label="Edit your profile"` is UNCHANGED on purpose —
    spec/system/profile_spec.rb and spec/system/profile_redesign_spec.rb both
    select on that label, not the icon.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.6) — this dialog is the forms family's reference
    screen, and most of it was already conformant. What changed:

    - The pencil trigger carried two Bootstrap-era class names left over from the
      retired SPA. Neither has a rule anywhere in the bundle, so both were dead; the
      button was being drawn entirely by the utilities beside them. They are replaced
      by what they were pretending to do — a bare, borderless, transparent control.
      A pointer cursor has to be asked for: Tailwind v4 no longer gives buttons one.
    - Every field gains the indigo focus border of TextField/TextAreaField. The boxed
      textarea (Headline) and the single-line inputs already carried the design
      system's field-border colour, which is the one thing the auth screens got wrong.
    - "Update photo" and "Save changes" go through `ds_button_classes` instead of two
      hand-typed strings: the `:outline` pill at the small size, and the solid pill the
      design system names for exactly this control ("Save changes" is its own example).
    - (Later than the rest of this list.) The header's X close goes through
      `ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "grey")` too, like its two siblings.
      Task 4.8 put the flag and challenge dialogs' X buttons
      on that helper and left this one on the hand-typed
      `text-<tone> fill-<tone> p-0 leading-none` it had carried since Task 4.6 — which
      meant that for one commit the three headers Dialog.prompt.md calls ONE component
      ("Flag this hoojah, Challenge @user to a debate, Edit your profile") were two shapes.
      Bringing this one across is a class-only change: same grey, same box, plus the house
      pointer cursor and press state, minus `leading-none` (the variant's `inline-flex`
      supersedes it). All three headers are byte-identical again apart from their id and
      their title.
    - "Private account" is Checkbox.prompt.md as it stood: a 16px NATIVE checkbox with
      a 14px grey label. There is no switch component in Hoojah and none is wanted.
    - The error panel is the FormError idiom — summarised at the top of the form, never
      annotated per field, and the only red in the product. It stays inline rather than
      rendering `devise/shared/_error_messages`, because that partial leads with a
      count heading this dialog has never shown, and the copy here is frozen.

    PHOTO UPLOAD (Track A, Cloudinary): the old client-side unsigned Cloudinary
    widget (an "Update photo" button + a hidden `user[photo]` field the widget filled,
    driven by the `cloudinary-upload` Stimulus controller) is gone. Photo upload is now
    a plain multipart `file_field :avatar` PATCHed to /u/:username, stored via
    ActiveStorage on the Cloudinary service. The form is multipart for that field.

    FROZEN: the PATCH to /u/:username, `dom_id(user, :edit_dialog)` (which
    `users/update.turbo_stream.erb` closes remotely), every `data-*` on the dialog,
    and every placeholder. %>
<% open = local_assigns.fetch(:open, false) %>
<div data-controller="dialog" class="<%= local_assigns.fetch(:wrapper_class, "") %>">
  <button type="button" data-action="dialog#open"
          class="flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 rounded-full border-0 bg-transparent text-white cursor-pointer"
          aria-label="Edit your profile">
    <%= lucide_icon("settings", class: "w-5 h-5") %>
  </button>

  <%# `open:flex` (NOT bare `flex`): author `display:flex` beats the UA
      `dialog:not([open]){display:none}` by origin, so a bare `flex` would keep the dialog
      on-screen while closed. The `open:` variant scopes the flex column to when the dialog
      is actually open; `max-h-[90dvh] overflow-hidden` cap it and the form body
      (`overflow-y-auto min-h-0`) scrolls under the pinned header. %>
  <dialog id="<%= dom_id(user, :edit_dialog) %>"
          data-dialog-target="dialog"
          data-action="click->dialog#backdropClose close->dialog#restoreFocus"
          aria-labelledby="dialog-title-profile-edit"
          <%= "open" if open %>
          class="rounded-lg shadow-lg p-0 w-full max-w-md backdrop:bg-black/40 max-h-[90dvh] overflow-hidden open:flex open:flex-col">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-3 border-b border-gray-100 shrink-0">
      <h5 id="dialog-title-profile-edit" class="text-lg font-medium m-0">Edit your profile</h5>
      <button type="button" data-action="dialog#close" aria-label="Close"
              class="<%= ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "grey") %>">
        <%= lucide_icon("x", class: "w-5 h-5") %>
      </button>
    </div>

    <%# The avatar uploader reuses the composer's image_upload controller INLINE (no nested
        <dialog>): chooser → live preview → DirectUpload progress → error/retry, mounted on
        this form. shape_label_value:"" suppresses the "16:9 crop" meta suffix (the avatar
        preview is circular, not a 16:9 crop). directUrl points at the same auth'd
        ActiveStorage endpoint the composer uses; the signed_id rides hujah-style in
        user[avatar], which user_params already permits as a scalar. %>
    <%= form_with model: user, url: profile_path(user.username), method: :patch,
          html: { multipart: true },
          data: { controller: "image-upload",
                  image_upload_direct_url_value: authenticated_direct_uploads_path,
                  image_upload_shape_label_value: "" },
          class: "p-4 overflow-y-auto min-h-0" do |f| %>
      <% if user.errors.any? %>
        <div class="mb-3 rounded bg-red-50 text-red-700 text-sm px-3 py-2">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-4 m-0">
            <% user.errors.full_messages.each do |msg| %><li><%= msg %></li><% end %>
          </ul>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <div class="flex flex-col items-center mb-4">
        <span class="block text-xs font-semibold text-faint mb-2">Photo</span>

        <%# Hidden signed_id field — this is what actually rides the PATCH (the file itself
            uploaded in the background). `value: nil` is load-bearing: with no value set,
            f.hidden_field would serialize the ActiveStorage::Attached object's to_s, so
            every no-change submit would post garbage and trip MessageVerifier. Same as the
            composer's hujah[image] field. %>
        <%= f.hidden_field :avatar, value: nil, data: { image_upload_target: "signedId" } %>

        <%# error banner (hidden by default; controller fills message + reveals) %>
        <div data-image-upload-target="error" hidden
             class="w-full flex items-start gap-3 px-3.5 py-3 rounded-lg bg-red-50 mb-3">
          <span class="text-red-700 flex-none"><%= lucide_icon("circle-alert", class: "w-5 h-5") %></span>
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <div data-image-upload-target="errorTitle" class="text-sm font-semibold text-red-700"></div>
            <div data-image-upload-target="errorBody" class="mt-0.5 text-xs leading-snug text-red-700/85"></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# CHOOSER (visible initially): current avatar + Change / Take a photo. No dialog. %>
        <div data-image-upload-target="chooser" class="flex flex-col items-center">
          <%# 96px `lg` avatar via `ui/_avatar` — `image_tag user.photo` raises on a blank
              photo, so the partial's fallback matters (a user who cleared their photo must
              still reach the editor). %>
          <%= render "ui/avatar", user: user, size: :lg, class: "mb-3" %>
          <div class="flex gap-2">
            <button type="button" data-action="image-upload#pickFile"
                    class="<%= ds_button_classes(variant: :outline, tone: "primary", size: :sm) %>">Change photo</button>
            <button type="button" data-action="image-upload#pickCamera"
                    class="<%= ds_button_classes(variant: :outline, tone: "grey", size: :sm) %>">Take a photo</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# PROGRESS (hidden): circular live preview + upload bar. %>
        <div data-image-upload-target="progress" hidden class="flex flex-col items-center w-full">
          <div class="relative w-24 h-24 rounded-full overflow-hidden bg-card-2">
            <img data-image-upload-target="progressPreview" alt="" class="w-full h-full object-cover">
            <span class="absolute inset-0 bg-white/35 pointer-events-none"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-3 w-full max-w-xs">
            <div class="flex justify-between text-xs font-bold text-ink-2"><span data-image-upload-target="progressName"></span><span data-image-upload-target="progressPct">0%</span></div>
            <div class="mt-1.5 h-2 rounded-full bg-field overflow-hidden"><div data-image-upload-target="progressBar" class="h-full rounded-full bg-primary" style="width:0%"></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# FAILED (hidden): network error + Retry / Choose another. %>
        <div data-image-upload-target="failed" hidden class="flex flex-col items-center w-full">
          <div class="w-24 h-24 rounded-full border border-dashed border-red-700 bg-card flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-1.5 text-center px-2">
            <span class="text-red-700"><%= lucide_icon("circle-alert", class: "w-5 h-5") %></span>
            <span data-image-upload-target="failedName" class="text-[10px] leading-tight text-faint"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex gap-2 mt-3">
            <button type="button" data-action="image-upload#retry" class="<%= ds_button_classes(tone: "primary", size: :sm) %>">Retry</button>
            <button type="button" data-action="image-upload#pickFile" class="<%= ds_button_classes(tone: "grey", size: :sm) %>">Choose another</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# ATTACHED (hidden): circular preview of the newly uploaded photo + Change / Remove.
            No alt-text field (avatars carry none), no triggerButton. %>
        <div data-image-upload-target="attached" hidden class="flex flex-col items-center w-full">
          <div class="w-24 h-24 rounded-full overflow-hidden bg-card-2">
            <img data-image-upload-target="attachedPreview" alt="" class="w-full h-full object-cover">
          </div>
          <div data-image-upload-target="attachedMeta" class="mt-2 text-xs text-faint"></div>
          <div class="flex gap-2 mt-2">
            <button type="button" data-action="image-upload#pickFile"
                    class="<%= ds_button_classes(variant: :outline, tone: "primary", size: :sm) %>">Change</button>
            <button type="button" data-action="image-upload#remove"
                    class="<%= ds_button_classes(variant: :outline, tone: "grey", size: :sm) %>">Remove</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# hidden file inputs (device + camera), wired exactly as _add_image_dialog. %>
        <input type="file" data-image-upload-target="fileInput" data-action="image-upload#fileChosen"
               accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/gif,image/webp" class="hidden">
        <input type="file" data-image-upload-target="cameraInput" data-action="image-upload#fileChosen"
               accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/gif,image/webp" capture="user" class="hidden">
      </div>

      <div class="mb-3">
        <%= f.label :full_name, "Full name", class: "block text-sm text-grey mb-1" %>
        <%= f.text_field :full_name, placeholder: "Your name",
              class: "w-full rounded border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 focus:outline-none focus:border-primary" %>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-3">
        <%= f.label :username, "User name", class: "block text-sm text-grey mb-1" %>
        <div class="flex">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center px-3 border border-r-0 border-gray-200 rounded-l bg-gray-50 text-grey">@</span>
          <%= f.text_field :username, placeholder: "Your @username",
                class: "w-full rounded-r border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 focus:outline-none focus:border-primary" %>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-3">
        <%= f.label :location, "Location", class: "block text-sm text-grey mb-1" %>
        <%= f.text_field :location, placeholder: "Where you're from",
              class: "w-full rounded border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 focus:outline-none focus:border-primary" %>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-3">
        <%= f.label :link, "Link", class: "block text-sm text-grey mb-1" %>
        <%= f.text_field :link, placeholder: "Your website",
              class: "w-full rounded border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 focus:outline-none focus:border-primary" %>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-4">
        <%= f.label :headline, "Headline", class: "block text-sm text-grey mb-1" %>
        <%= f.text_area :headline, rows: 3, placeholder: "Add some jazz to your profile!",
              class: "w-full resize-none rounded border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 focus:outline-none focus:border-primary" %>
      </div>

      <%# Slice 7b: private-account toggle. When ON, new follows become requests you
          approve; when flipped back OFF, all pending requests are auto-accepted. %>
      <div class="mb-4">
        <label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-grey">
          <%= f.check_box :private, class: "w-4 h-4" %>
          <span>Private account — approve followers before they see your hoojahs</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <%# Issue #3: opt out of email delivery. The in-app notification still fires;
          this only silences the high-signal email copy (mentions, debates, moderation). %>
      <div class="mb-4">
        <label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-grey">
          <%= f.check_box :email_notifications, class: "w-4 h-4" %>
          <span>Email me about mentions, debates and moderation</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="text-right">
        <%= f.submit "Save changes", class: ds_button_classes(variant: :solid) %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </dialog>
</div>
